<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Those Who Hunt Goblins, 1973</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;The USN vs. Soviet Submarines in the&amp;nbsp;Northwest Atlantic Ocean.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Version 1.1 for CMANO Build 839&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;West of&amp;nbsp;Bermuda, 9 October 1973.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;October 1973&amp;nbsp;is a time of&amp;nbsp;increasing tension between the United States and the Soviet Union.&amp;nbsp; Russia's proxy Egypt and her Arab allies are at war with America's proxy Israel and the latter has suffered some significant defeats.&amp;nbsp; Both&amp;nbsp;the USN&amp;nbsp;and Red Banner Fleets&amp;nbsp;have rushed naval reinforcements into the Med and with the two navies operating at close proximity, the possibility for accident or opportunity sneak attack&amp;nbsp;is considered very great.&amp;nbsp; For the first time since the 1962 Cuban Missile Crisis the US has set DEFCON-3 while ships of&amp;nbsp;both sides play an ever more&amp;nbsp;serious game of cat and mouse, frequently illuminating their opponents with fire control radars&amp;nbsp;while training weapon mounts&amp;nbsp;at each other's ships and planes.&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Fortunately, for the most part the agreed conventions for incidents at sea&amp;nbsp;are working&amp;nbsp;as&amp;nbsp;intended while cool heads are preventing shots from being fired&amp;nbsp;and the expansion of the crisis.&amp;nbsp; The diplomats are&amp;nbsp;still talking&amp;nbsp;and so far there has been no escalation outside the region while the channels of communications between Washington and Moscow remain open.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;At this particular moment in time America's strategic posture is badly out of balance as virtually all the available aircraft carriers are deployed off Southeast Asia or in support of operations in the Middle East with the Sixth Fleet and NATO contingency deployments in the North East Atlantic.&amp;nbsp; The only significant naval force to protect the Eastern Seaboard of the United States is the &lt;EM&gt;Intrepid &lt;/EM&gt;Battle Group with her hybrid air group and ad hoc collection of escorts.&amp;nbsp; This would not normally be an issue but the crisis in the Med has siphoned off most of the SSN's that normally track and trail the Soviet SSBN's operating in the Western Atlantic.&amp;nbsp; At least three Soviet nuclear submarines, two of them believed to be &lt;EM&gt;Yankee&lt;/EM&gt; SSBN's are operating between Bermuda and the coast and under normal circumstances American SSN's are tasked with locating and tracking the Soviet missile boats.&amp;nbsp; However, &lt;EM&gt;USS Finback &lt;/EM&gt;(&lt;EM&gt;SSN-670&lt;/EM&gt;)&amp;nbsp;has been forced to return to base and has dropped the goblin she was tracking.&amp;nbsp; Meanwhile a series of&amp;nbsp;operations-related incidents have caused the&amp;nbsp;Orion sorties from NAS Bermuda to lose track of their goblin that had formally been tracked by &lt;EM&gt;USS Pogy (SSN-647)&lt;/EM&gt; now transiting to Gibraltar.&amp;nbsp; Tensions between the USA and USSR have not been greater in eleven-years and now the plots for at least two Soviet ballistic missile submarines operating uncomfortably close to America have been lost.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You are Commanding Officer of the &lt;EM&gt;Intrepid &lt;/EM&gt;Battle Group.&amp;nbsp; Your force had been exercising with Canadian and British ASW forces south of Halifax when a priority operational action message caused you to break off the training and transit to the vicinity of Bermuda at high speed.&amp;nbsp; You have just completed a RAS and detailed orders have been received.&amp;nbsp; &lt;EM&gt;Intrepid's&lt;/EM&gt; air wing is unique as she had formally been classified &lt;EM&gt;CVA-11&lt;/EM&gt; with an attack role but after her last deployment off Vietnam most of her strike aircraft were replaced with ASW assets and she was redesignated as &lt;EM&gt;CV-11&lt;/EM&gt;.&amp;nbsp; She is scheduled to be decommissioned some time in 1974 but right now she is what's available to defend the east coast of the United States.&amp;nbsp; Your escorts are a mixed bag, some new and still working up, some old and&amp;nbsp;in the hands of&amp;nbsp;reservists.&amp;nbsp; One is &lt;EM&gt;USS Glover AGDE-1&lt;/EM&gt;, an ASW trials ship that had been sent to work with the NATO allies but has been ordered to remain with your command for this operation.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In addition to detailed orders, your briefing contains the initial operational action message plus three consolidated intelligence summaries (INTSUM's) that have been received during the transit south.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Although DEFCON-3 is in effect, peacetime rules of engagement remain in force.&amp;nbsp; You may shoot in self-defence against targets of any type positively identified as hostile &lt;U&gt;after&lt;/U&gt; they have exhibited definite hostile intent towards units under your command.&amp;nbsp; An overflight of your vessels by a military aircraft even if visibly armed is considered an unfriendly act rather than a hostile one. You may shoot at any unidentified submarine that has launched or is launching ballistic missiles against any target in the Americas.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;A status of Weapons Hold is in effect and no live munitions are to be directed against any contact or unit not meeting hostile unit criteria detailed above without authorization from CINCLANT.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario Designer's Notes:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;ASW was a significant role for US and NATO navies during the Cold War.&amp;nbsp; From a gaming standpoint these sorts of scenarios are sometimes considered boring; "Watching Paint Dry" held as an apt descriptor for anti-submarine warfare scenarios in general.&amp;nbsp; Tiresome perhaps, but necessary and also prone to the classic paradigm of most combat situations, that being hours of tedium punctuated by moments of absolute terror.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;However I usually find gaming ASW situations challenging, technically fascinating and endlessly frustrating and so cooked up this hypothetical situation in the North Atlantic with an eye towards the real geopolitical situation as I understand it was at the time.&amp;nbsp; The CMANO event editor and the ability to configure side postures provides fertile ground for the "Not Quite War and yet Not Really Peace" scenario, at least that's the intention and it is entirely up to the Player to determine if that goal has been achieved.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In 1973 and with all eyes focused on the Arab-Israeli war, most&amp;nbsp;civilians never knew of the military crisis between America and the Soviet Union that was developing in the Eastern Med.&amp;nbsp; The personal realities of coping with the fallout from the OPEC oil embargo and the subsequent gas&amp;nbsp;shortages at the&amp;nbsp;local pumps diverted public attention from the building superpower confrontation.&amp;nbsp; Fortunately all ended without the conflict widening but with hindsight it's easy to think that it may have been otherwise.&amp;nbsp; Your ROE reflect this and are worded so as not to completely prevent you from acting in self defence but their intentions are clear and unambiguous: you are NOT to start shooting without orders except in the immediate defence of forces under your command or the CONUS.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The lack of strategic balance&amp;nbsp;in United States&amp;nbsp;deployments in October 1973 was real and as near as I could determine the only aircraft carrier&amp;nbsp;on the&amp;nbsp;Atlantic seaboard was indeed &lt;EM&gt;USS Intrepid, CV-11&lt;/EM&gt; with&amp;nbsp;her composite airgroup and due to be decommissioned by the end of the fiscal year.&amp;nbsp; Particularly during crisis periods, both sides constantly&amp;nbsp;attempted to monitor the other sides'&amp;nbsp;ballistic missile submarines with various degrees of success and at this time the USN had the technological advantage.&amp;nbsp; However now circumstances have peeled away the&amp;nbsp;submarine trackers&amp;nbsp;and with&amp;nbsp;political tensions on a knife edge ASW has once again become a priority, particularly if something should go wrong.&amp;nbsp; Now this WW2 veteran&amp;nbsp;and her old Trackers&amp;nbsp;with a fiscal Sword of Damocles hanging over her very existence is America's&amp;nbsp;first line of defence.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Enjoy.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;-C&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
